From 1dde984a641c79c8db01328060f39da50d176ee6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 19:40:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 077/113] rust: drm: kms: mark the mode-object macro sketch as
 non-test

The impl_from_opaque_mode_obj! documentation is deliberately schematic: it contains an ellipsis placeholder and refers to the private macro without importing its surrounding types.

The kernel KUnit doctest extractor cannot execute compile-fail tests. It treats the custom test builder succeeding as the snippet unexpectedly compiling, so CONFIG_RUST_KERNEL_DOCTESTS currently fails while processing this example.

Mark the sketch ignored, matching its illustrative purpose and allowing the real kernel doctests to be generated.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-0
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
Signed-off-by: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
---
 rust/kernel/drm/kms.rs | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/rust/kernel/drm/kms.rs b/rust/kernel/drm/kms.rs
index c89e3cd5bda1..c10b2488af9b 100644
--- a/rust/kernel/drm/kms.rs
+++ b/rust/kernel/drm/kms.rs
@@ -77,7 +77,7 @@ unsafe fn setup_kms(_drm: &Device<Self::Driver>) -> Result<ModeConfigInfo> {
 /// generate said functions for any kind of type which the original mode object driver trait can be
 /// derived from. All conversions check the mode object's vtable. For example:
 ///
-/// ```compile_fail
+/// ```ignore
 /// impl<'a, T: DriverConnectorState> ConnectorState<T> {
 ///     impl_from_opaque_mode_obj! {
 ///         // | An optional lifetime and param-variables to declare for each function
